[38;2;124;124;124mCounts: (0,0):3, (0,1):1, (1,0):2, (1,1):0.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor 270° CW at (0,0): (0,0),(0,1),(0,2),(1,0),(2,0),(2,1).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(0,0)→(0,0), (0,1)→(0,1), (0,2)→(0,0), (1,0)→(1,0), (2,0)→(0,0), (2,1)→(0,1).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mCounts: (0,0):3, (0,1):2, (1,0):1, (1,1):0.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor H-flip at (0,0): (0,2),(1,0),(1,2),(2,0),(2,1),(2,2).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(0,2)→(0,0), (1,0)→(1,0), (1,2)→(1,0), (2,0)→(0,0), (2,1)→(0,1), (2,2)→(0,0).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mCounts: (0,0):3, (0,1):1, (1,0):2, (1,1):0.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor V-flip at (0,0): (0,0),(0,1),(0,2),(1,0),(1,2),(2,0).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(0,0)→(0,0), (0,1)→(0,1), (0,2)→(0,0), (1,0)→(1,0), (1,2)→(1,0), (2,0)→(0,0).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mCounts: (0,0):3, (0,1):1, (1,0):2, (1,1):0.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor main diag at (0,0): (0,0),(0,1),(1,0),(2,0),(2,1),(2,2).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(0,0)→(0,0), (0,1)→(0,1), (1,0)→(1,0), (2,0)→(0,0), (2,1)→(0,1), (2,2)→(0,0).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mCounts: (0,0):3, (0,1):2, (1,0):1, (1,1):0.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor anti-diag at (0,0): (0,0),(0,1),(0,2),(1,2),(2,1),(2,2).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(0,0)→(0,0), (0,1)→(0,1), (0,2)→(0,0), (1,2)→(1,0), (2,1)→(0,1), (2,2)→(0,0).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mCounts: (0,0):3, (0,1):2, (1,0):1, (1,1):0.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the 4-color counts are always (3, *, *, 0) where (0,0) gets 3 and (1,1) gets [0m[38;2;124;124;124m0. The * are either (1,2) or (2,1) for (0,1) and (1,0).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mBut the hook can be at any position (r,c), so the 4-color pattern shifts. The [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcolor of cell (r+i, c+j) is ((r+i) mod 2, (c+j) mod 2) = ((r mod 2 + i mod 2) [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mmod 2, (c mod 2 + j mod 2) mod 2). So the 4-color counts are a permutation [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mdepending on (r mod 2, c mod 2).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe key observation: (1,1) always gets 0 cells. This means the hook never covers[0m[38;2;124;124;124ma cell with color (1,1) relative to its bounding box. But (1,1) relative to the [0m[38;2;124;124;124mbounding box at (r,c) is the cell (r+1, c+1), which is the center of the 3×3 [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mblock. And the center is always removed! So this is trivially true and doesn't [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mgive an obstruction.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mHowever, the 4-coloring of the whole rectangle does give information. Let me [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcompute the 4-color counts for the m×n rectangle.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor an m×n rectangle, the number of cells of color (a,b) where a = i mod 2, b = [0m[38;2;124;124;124mj mod 2:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- N_{0,0} = ceil(m/2) * ceil(n/2)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- N_{0,1} = ceil(m/2) * floor(n/2)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- N_{1,0} = floor(m/2) * ceil(n/2)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- N_{1,1} = floor(m/2) * floor(n/2)[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mEach hook contributes 3 to one color, 0 to the opposite color, and 1+2 to the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mremaining two. The color getting 3 is determined by (r mod 2, c mod 2), and the [0m[38;2;124;124;124mcolor getting 0 is the opposite.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSpecifically, if the hook is at position (r,c) with r mod 2 = α, c mod 2 = β:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- Color (α, β) gets 3[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- Color (1-α, 1-β) gets 0[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- Colors (α, 1-β) and (1-α, β) get 1 and 2 (in some order)[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo each hook contributes 3 to color (α,β), 0 to (1-α,1-β), and 1+2=3 to the [0m
