[38;2;124;124;124mLet me try colorings based on roots of unity of higher order. Let me try w(r,c) [0m[38;2;124;124;124m= ω^r where ω = e^{2πi/4} = i. This is the 4-periodic row coloring.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor m ≡ 2 mod 4: Σ_{r=0}^{m-1} i^r = 1 + i + (-1) + (-i) + ... + 1 + i = (1+i) *[0m[38;2;124;124;124m(m/4) + ... wait, m = 4k+2, so Σ = (1+i-1-i)*k + 1 + i = 1 + i.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mS = (1+i) * n.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor n ≡ 2 mod 4: S = (1+i)(1+i) = (1+i)^2 = 2i.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mHook sum at row r with row counts (a,b,c): i^r * (a + bi + c*i^2) = i^r * ((a-c)[0m[38;2;124;124;124m+ bi).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mPossible values of (a-c) + bi where (a,b,c) is a permutation of (1,2,3):[0m
[38;2;124;124;124ma-c ∈ {-2,-1,0,1,2} and b ∈ {1,2,3}.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mBut not all combinations are possible. Let me list:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(1,2,3): -2+2i[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(1,3,2): -1+3i[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(2,1,3): -1+1i[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(2,3,1): 1+3i[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(3,1,2): 1+1i[0m
