[38;2;124;124;124mThe hook is a 3×3 square with 3 cells removed: the center, the middle of one [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mside, and an adjacent corner. The 3 removed cells form an L-tromino.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mKey observation: the center of the 3×3 block is always removed. This means that [0m[38;2;124;124;124min a tiling, the center of each hook's 3×3 block is covered by a different hook.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about this "center-covering" relationship. Each hook H at position [0m[38;2;124;124;124m(r,c) has its center at (r+1, c+1). This center must be covered by another hook [0m[38;2;124;124;124mH'. H' must be at a position (r', c') such that (r+1, c+1) is in H's 3×3 block [0m
