[38;2;124;124;124mand c' ∈ {c-1, c, c+1}. But also (r+1, c+1) must be one of the 6 cells of H', [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mnot one of the 3 removed cells.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis creates a dependency graph between hooks. Maybe this graph structure can be[0m[38;2;124;124;124mexploited.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually, let me try a different approach. Let me look at the problem from the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mperspective of the "signed area" or "moment" constraints.[0m

